{%- comment -%}
  Relates the prize value to the entry price in one line.

  Both numbers are already on the page, but they sit in different blocks and the
  customer is left to do the arithmetic. "£529 prize · £2.49 an entry" states the
  comparison the entry price is actually asking them to make. It is two facts
  the store already publishes, put next to each other — not a claim about value,
  a saving, or a likelihood of winning.

  Deliberately not included: any "worth X times the entry" multiplier. That
  framing invites the reader to treat an entry as an investment with an expected
  return, which is both misleading and the exact register this brand avoids.

  Parameters:
    product  (required)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign prize_value = product.metafields.custom.prize_value
  assign show = false
  if prize_value != blank
    if product.price > 0
      assign show = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if show -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign prize_text = prize_value.value | money | remove: '.00'
    if product.price_varies
      assign entry_text = product.price_min | money
    else
      assign entry_text = product.price | money
    endif
  -%}
  <p class="competition-anchor">
    {{- 'products.competition.anchor' | t: prize: prize_text, entry: entry_text -}}
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
